+# Incident brief
+
+Action status as of the 30 September on-call meeting.
+
+## 11 August 2026: ingest stall and full disk
+
+- **Impact:** About two and a half hours overnight without new data; customers saw stale dashboards. No data lost.
+- **Cause:** One malformed batch jammed ingest; endless retries filled the database disk with logs, briefly blocking writes.
+- **Fix:** Restarted ingest with the bad batch set aside; freed disk space.
+- **Actions:**
+  - Disk alert at 80%: Sunil, done.
+  - Stop bad batches jamming ingest: Jonas, open (in review).
+  - Faster paging escalation (15 minutes): Elif and Sunil, done.
+
+## 21 September 2026: expired API certificate
+
+- **Impact:** 47 minutes on a Monday morning when nearly all customers and integrations could not reach the public API.
+- **Cause:** The API's security certificate expired; its automatic renewal had silently failed for weeks, using an outdated credential.
+- **Fix:** Renewed the certificate, restarted the API; renewal is repaired and now alerts on failure.
+- **Actions:**
+  - Reminder 14 days before each expiry: Priya, done.
+  - Alert on days left before expiry: Priya, open.
+  - Certificate check in weekly checklist: Tomasz, open.
+  - Responders record their actions during incidents: Mara, done.
